1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:03,795
Look closely at the walls around the Great Sphinx.

2
00:00:03,795 --> 00:00:05,319
Deep vertical grooves.

3
00:00:05,319 --> 00:00:06,427
Rounded hollows.

4
00:00:06,427 --> 00:00:11,066
Rock that looks as if it has been rained on for thousands of years.

5
00:00:11,533 --> 00:00:14,592
Some people say that is exactly what happened.

6
00:00:14,592 --> 00:00:20,178
That the Sphinx is not four and a half thousand years old, but ten thousand or more.

7
00:00:20,178 --> 00:00:24,766
Carved by a lost civilization, maybe with help from beyond our world.

8
00:00:25,233 --> 00:00:26,869
Egyptologists say no.

9
00:00:26,869 --> 00:00:32,558
It was carved by the workers of a pharaoh, around twenty five hundred BC.

10
00:00:32,558 --> 00:00:33,805
So who is right?

11
00:00:33,805 --> 00:00:35,286
A rock cannot talk.

12
00:00:35,286 --> 00:00:36,766
But it can be read.

13
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:41,962
Tonight we read the Sphinx the way a geologist reads a drill core.

14
00:00:41,962 --> 00:00:43,682
From the top layer down.

15
00:00:43,682 --> 00:00:46,333
Each layer is one period of its life.

16
00:00:50,799 --> 00:00:52,351
First, the briefing.

17
00:00:52,351 --> 00:00:55,376
October nineteen ninety-one, San Diego.

18
00:00:55,376 --> 00:01:03,600
At the Geological Society of America, a Boston University geologist named Robert Schoch drops a bombshell.

19
00:01:04,066 --> 00:01:08,709
He says the weathering on the Sphinx enclosure was made by rain.

20
00:01:08,709 --> 00:01:09,942
Long, heavy rain.

21
00:01:09,942 --> 00:01:15,673
And that means the Sphinx dates to between seven thousand and five thousand BC.

22
00:01:15,673 --> 00:01:20,533
And I am trying to be conservative, he tells the Los Angeles Times.

23
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,665
Archaeologists push back immediately.

24
00:01:23,665 --> 00:01:29,067
An archaeologist at Berkeley says: there is just no way that could be true.

25
00:01:29,067 --> 00:01:31,299
The fight is still going today.

26
00:01:31,766 --> 00:01:33,687
And others go much further.

27
00:01:33,687 --> 00:01:42,863
Writers in the nineteen nineties claim the Sphinx was begun in ten thousand five hundred BC, built to face the constellation Leo.

28
00:01:42,863 --> 00:01:46,633
Others link it to Atlantis, or to ancient astronauts.

29
00:01:47,099 --> 00:01:49,179
So we have two birth dates.

30
00:01:49,179 --> 00:01:52,413
Old Kingdom, about twenty five hundred BC.

31
00:01:52,413 --> 00:01:55,647
Or ten thousand five hundred BC and older.

32
00:01:55,647 --> 00:01:57,033
Let us drill down.

33
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:59,617
Layer one is the modern skin.

34
00:01:59,617 --> 00:02:05,384
In eighteen seventeen the Italian explorer Caviglia dug out the Sphinx's chest.

35
00:02:05,384 --> 00:02:12,100
From nineteen twenty-five to nineteen thirty-six, Émile Baraize cleared the whole enclosure.

36
00:02:12,566 --> 00:02:16,127
In nineteen twenty-six part of the headdress fell off.

37
00:02:16,127 --> 00:02:21,599
In nineteen thirty-one engineers repaired the head and neck with a concrete collar.

38
00:02:22,066 --> 00:02:27,215
In the nineteen eighties and nineties, restorers patched the base and body again.

39
00:02:27,215 --> 00:02:30,966
In nineteen eighty-eight, a chunk of the shoulder fell off.

40
00:02:31,433 --> 00:02:43,966
Before those repairs, a young American named Mark Lehner mapped the Sphinx stone by stone from nineteen seventy-nine to eighty-three, standing on ledges a foot wide, three stories up.

41
00:02:44,433 --> 00:02:45,964
And here is the twist.

42
00:02:45,964 --> 00:02:50,278
That mapping project was funded by the Edgar Cayce Foundation.

43
00:02:50,278 --> 00:02:55,706
Cayce was the psychic who said the Sphinx was built by refugees from Atlantis.

44
00:02:55,706 --> 00:02:59,533
The believers paid for the survey that would test them.

45
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,891
First lesson from layer one.

46
00:03:01,891 --> 00:03:05,133
The surface you see today is not ancient at all.

47
00:03:05,599 --> 00:03:07,810
Layer two: patches of empire.

48
00:03:07,810 --> 00:03:12,078
Lehner found three ancient skins of masonry on the body.

49
00:03:12,078 --> 00:03:19,166
The outermost, made of small stones almost the size of bricks, probably dates to Roman times.

50
00:03:19,633 --> 00:03:24,631
The Romans built a stairway down to the paws so visitors could admire it.

51
00:03:24,631 --> 00:03:28,533
Pliny the Elder even wrote that its face was painted red.

52
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:37,085
Under the Roman layer sits a middle skin of medium slabs, probably from the Saite kings, around six hundred BC.

53
00:03:37,085 --> 00:03:40,800
It kept falling apart, so people kept repairing it.

54
00:03:41,266 --> 00:03:43,313
Even the word sphinx is late.

55
00:03:43,313 --> 00:03:48,537
The Greeks gave it that name about two thousand years after it was carved.

56
00:03:48,537 --> 00:03:52,066
So far, the layers only tell us how old it is not.

57
00:03:52,533 --> 00:03:54,463
Layer three: the dream king.

58
00:03:54,463 --> 00:03:58,048
After the Old Kingdom collapsed, Giza was abandoned.

59
00:03:58,048 --> 00:04:01,633
Drifting sand buried the Sphinx up to its shoulders.

60
00:04:02,099 --> 00:04:07,969
Around fourteen hundred BC, a young prince named Thutmose fell asleep in its shadow.

61
00:04:07,969 --> 00:04:13,699
The Sphinx spoke to him in a dream: clear away the sand, and I will make you king.

62
00:04:14,166 --> 00:04:20,033
He became Thutmose the fourth, dug out the paws, and set up this: the Dream Stela.

63
00:04:20,033 --> 00:04:22,966
Red granite, three point six metres tall.

64
00:04:23,433 --> 00:04:24,902
Now look at its back.

65
00:04:24,902 --> 00:04:27,142
Pivot sockets for a wooden door.

66
00:04:27,142 --> 00:04:33,300
The stela is a recycled door lintel, dragged here from the temple of the pharaoh Khafre.

67
00:04:33,766 --> 00:04:36,720
Its text once held part of a royal name.

68
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:41,740
Early scholars read the syllable Khaf, and restored the name Khafre.

69
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:45,727
But by nineteen twenty-five that line had flaked away.

70
00:04:45,727 --> 00:04:47,500
A clue, not a signature.

71
00:04:47,966 --> 00:04:50,594
Here is the key finding of layer three.

72
00:04:50,594 --> 00:05:00,766
Lehner showed that the deep erosion of the Sphinx's body was already there before the New Kingdom masons covered it with their first big casing stones.

73
00:05:01,233 --> 00:05:06,090
So the damage happened between the carving and about fourteen hundred BC.

74
00:05:06,090 --> 00:05:07,421
Is that enough time?

75
00:05:07,421 --> 00:05:14,941
Zahi Hawass says eleven hundred years, or even half that, would be more than enough for this soft layer to erode.

76
00:05:14,941 --> 00:05:19,066
The believers say only thousands of years of rain could do it.

77
00:05:19,533 --> 00:05:21,083
Layer four: the quarry.

78
00:05:21,083 --> 00:05:22,768
The Sphinx was not built.

79
00:05:22,768 --> 00:05:28,633
It was cut, by quarrying away the bedrock around a core of rock that was left standing.

80
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:33,572
And the stone that came out went straight into the temple in front of it.

81
00:05:33,572 --> 00:05:35,899
Core blocks of up to one hundred tons.

82
00:05:36,366 --> 00:05:44,019
Geologists Thomas Aigner and Lal Gauri logged every rock layer in the Sphinx and every block in the temple.

83
00:05:44,019 --> 00:05:45,235
The layers match.

84
00:05:45,235 --> 00:05:51,099
Some run continuously from one block to the next, just as they ran in the bedrock.

85
00:05:51,566 --> 00:05:52,627
Now the layout.

86
00:05:52,627 --> 00:05:58,072
The Sphinx Temple was built on top of the old wall of Khafre's Valley Temple.

87
00:05:58,072 --> 00:06:04,366
And the south wall of the Sphinx enclosure follows the slanted line of Khafre's causeway.

88
00:06:04,833 --> 00:06:05,792
Then the trash.

89
00:06:05,792 --> 00:06:16,600
In the lowest debris, Hawass and Lehner found the builders' pottery, flint flakes, and a quartzite hammerstone with copper flecks, where a worker struck a copper chisel.

90
00:06:17,066 --> 00:06:19,208
And the job was never finished.

91
00:06:19,208 --> 00:06:25,633
The enclosure walls are cut unevenly, and the temple's granite casing was only partly fitted.

92
00:06:26,100 --> 00:06:32,251
Luminescence dating of the two temples gives the middle to late third millennium BC.

93
00:06:32,251 --> 00:06:35,399
The same window as Khafre and the pyramids.

94
00:06:35,866 --> 00:06:36,723
But be fair.

95
00:06:36,723 --> 00:06:43,292
In nineteen forty-nine the Egyptian archaeologist Selim Hassan admitted something important.

96
00:06:43,292 --> 00:06:49,433
There is not one single contemporary inscription that connects the Sphinx with Khafre.

97
00:06:49,899 --> 00:06:57,764
Some experts even argue for his father Khufu, or his brother Djedefre, based on the headdress style and the causeway.

98
00:06:57,764 --> 00:07:00,385
Notice where that debate lives, though.

99
00:07:00,385 --> 00:07:04,216
It is a fight over a few decades inside the same dynasty.

100
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:06,233
Not over eight thousand years.

101
00:07:06,699 --> 00:07:08,778
Layer five: the rock itself.

102
00:07:08,778 --> 00:07:15,089
The Sphinx is carved from limestone laid down on a sea floor fifty million years ago.

103
00:07:15,089 --> 00:07:18,133
Hard and soft bands, stacked like a cake.

104
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:22,476
This is where the water theory makes its strongest case.

105
00:07:22,476 --> 00:07:30,646
Schoch points to the rounded, undulating profile of the enclosure walls, and vertical fissures that run down the rock.

106
00:07:30,646 --> 00:07:33,138
Wind cuts horizontal lines, he says.

107
00:07:33,138 --> 00:07:34,800
Rain cuts vertical ones.

108
00:07:35,266 --> 00:07:37,168
Then his strangest evidence.

109
00:07:37,168 --> 00:07:44,501
With geophysicist Thomas Dobecki, he hit the enclosure floor with a sledgehammer and listened to the echoes.

110
00:07:44,501 --> 00:07:49,323
In front and on the sides, the rock is weathered about eight feet deep.

111
00:07:49,323 --> 00:07:51,699
Behind the Sphinx, only about four.

112
00:07:52,166 --> 00:07:59,359
His reading: the front was cut first, thousands of years earlier, and the back was cut later under Khafre.

113
00:07:59,359 --> 00:08:07,366
He first dated the core to before five thousand BC, and later pushed it back to around nine thousand seven hundred BC.

114
00:08:07,833 --> 00:08:09,677
Now the cross-examination.

115
00:08:09,677 --> 00:08:11,096
Objection one: salt.

116
00:08:11,096 --> 00:08:14,500
The Sphinx sits just above the Nile water table.

117
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:20,104
Moisture climbs into the stone, salts crystallize, and the surface flakes away.

118
00:08:20,104 --> 00:08:26,133
The Getty Conservation Institute concluded salt explains at least some of the damage.

119
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:29,491
Geologist Lal Gauri blamed salts and dew.

120
00:08:29,491 --> 00:08:35,133
James Harrell blamed wet sand that filled the enclosure for most of its history.

121
00:08:35,133 --> 00:08:40,000
Others note the fissures were in the bedrock before anyone carved it.

122
00:08:40,466 --> 00:08:43,186
Objection two: the rain did not stop.

123
00:08:43,186 --> 00:08:54,066
Excavations at Saqqara, next door, show torrential rains and sheet floods hitting tombs at the end of the Old Kingdom, around twenty two hundred BC.

124
00:08:54,533 --> 00:08:57,815
And Giza still gets the occasional downpour today.

125
00:08:57,815 --> 00:09:05,299
Schoch's critics say he never showed why four and a half thousand years of storms could not round off those walls.

126
00:09:05,766 --> 00:09:09,116
Then there is a third geologist, Colin Reader.

127
00:09:09,116 --> 00:09:14,722
He agrees water did it, but water running off the plateau into the enclosure.

128
00:09:14,722 --> 00:09:20,839
And he concludes the Sphinx could be older than Khafre, but only by a few centuries.

129
00:09:20,839 --> 00:09:22,368
Early dynastic Egypt.

130
00:09:22,368 --> 00:09:23,533
Not the Ice Age.

131
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:31,274
So layer five gives the water theory its best point: the weathering is real, and its cause is still argued.

132
00:09:31,274 --> 00:09:34,674
But no layer of rock carries a date written on it.

133
00:09:34,674 --> 00:09:36,577
Erosion rates are estimates.

134
00:09:36,577 --> 00:09:39,433
Pottery and stratigraphy are measurements.

135
00:09:39,899 --> 00:09:41,697
Layer six: bedrock zero.

136
00:09:41,697 --> 00:09:43,869
Ten thousand five hundred BC.

137
00:09:43,869 --> 00:09:45,966
Is there anything down here?

138
00:09:46,433 --> 00:09:57,135
The Leo claim says that in ten thousand five hundred BC, the lion constellation rose due east at the spring equinox, right where the Sphinx looks.

139
00:09:57,135 --> 00:09:58,894
But astronomers checked.

140
00:09:58,894 --> 00:10:02,633
At that date the equinox sun sat in Virgo, not Leo.

141
00:10:03,100 --> 00:10:06,799
And the zodiac lion itself came from Mesopotamia.

142
00:10:06,799 --> 00:10:14,500
Egypt did not use those constellations until the Greek and Roman era, thousands of years after Khafre.

143
00:10:14,966 --> 00:10:22,674
Edgar Cayce promised a Hall of Records from Atlantis under the Sphinx, to be found in nineteen ninety-eight.

144
00:10:22,674 --> 00:10:25,243
Nineteen ninety-eight came and went.

145
00:10:25,243 --> 00:10:30,595
The flooded Osiris shaft nearby was fully explored in nineteen ninety-nine.

146
00:10:30,595 --> 00:10:31,166
Nothing.

147
00:10:31,633 --> 00:10:33,945
Now the believers' best card.

148
00:10:33,945 --> 00:10:35,858
Göbekli Tepe, in Turkey.

149
00:10:35,858 --> 00:10:40,722
Monumental stone circles built around ninety five hundred BC.

150
00:10:40,722 --> 00:10:45,266
So yes, hunter-gatherers did build big things that early.

151
00:10:45,733 --> 00:10:52,815
But Göbekli Tepe is more than a thousand kilometres away, and its pillars are a few metres tall.

152
00:10:52,815 --> 00:11:00,339
Around Giza, there is no trace of a society that could carve a seventy-three metre statue in that era.

153
00:11:00,339 --> 00:11:03,733
No towns, no bakeries, no workers' cemeteries.

154
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,693
And the alien version?

155
00:11:05,693 --> 00:11:13,566
There is no tool, no material and no inscription anywhere in the Sphinx's layers that points to visitors from space.

156
00:11:14,033 --> 00:11:16,999
But there is one real surprise down here.

157
00:11:16,999 --> 00:11:25,535
In twenty twenty-three, scientists at New York University put clay mounds with hard lumps inside in a fast water flow.

158
00:11:25,535 --> 00:11:30,600
The mounds eroded into lion-like shapes, with a head, a neck and paws.

159
00:11:31,066 --> 00:11:34,943
Desert ridges like this are called yardangs, or mud lions.

160
00:11:34,943 --> 00:11:39,955
So maybe the oldest thing about the Sphinx is not the statue, but the rock.

161
00:11:39,955 --> 00:11:44,299
Nature may have started the shape, and the Egyptians finished it.

162
00:11:44,766 --> 00:11:46,150
Core sample complete.

163
00:11:46,150 --> 00:11:47,600
Here is the scorecard.

164
00:11:48,066 --> 00:11:51,780
The enclosure walls are deeply weathered: evidence.

165
00:11:51,780 --> 00:11:55,129
Only centuries of rain could do it: contested.

166
00:11:55,129 --> 00:11:58,915
Heavy rain ended before three thousand BC: debunked.

167
00:11:58,915 --> 00:12:03,866
The Sphinx and its temples were cut in one quarry project: evidence.

168
00:12:04,333 --> 00:12:09,130
Carved in ten thousand five hundred BC to face Leo: debunked.

169
00:12:09,130 --> 00:12:11,961
Lost or alien builders: no evidence.

170
00:12:11,961 --> 00:12:15,499
Which king of the fourth dynasty: still open.

171
00:12:15,966 --> 00:12:16,846
The verdict.

172
00:12:16,846 --> 00:12:27,766
The Sphinx belongs to the Old Kingdom, around twenty five hundred BC, most likely to Khafre's building project, with Khufu as the main rival suspect.

173
00:12:28,233 --> 00:12:33,124
The water erosion is real, and it is a genuine geological puzzle.

174
00:12:33,124 --> 00:12:41,626
But the most generous geologist on the believers' side, Colin Reader, only stretches the date by a few centuries.

175
00:12:41,626 --> 00:12:43,733
Not by eight thousand years.

176
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:48,337
The ten thousand five hundred BC date did not come from the rock.

177
00:12:48,337 --> 00:12:55,466
It came from a psychic's reading in the nineteen thirties, and from a constellation that was in the wrong place.

178
00:12:55,933 --> 00:12:58,351
And notice who settled most of this.

179
00:12:58,351 --> 00:13:04,933
People with drawing boards, hand lenses and sledgehammers, measuring the rock one layer at a time.

180
00:13:05,399 --> 00:13:09,279
The Sphinx is still eroding today, a little every year.

181
00:13:09,279 --> 00:13:13,089
It does not need aliens or Atlantis to be astonishing.

182
00:13:13,089 --> 00:13:20,566
It is a mountain of rock that people turned into a god, and then spent four thousand years trying to save.

183
00:13:21,033 --> 00:13:22,603
That is the core sample.

184
00:13:22,603 --> 00:13:24,892
Old Kingdom, or ten thousand years?

185
00:13:24,892 --> 00:13:31,433
Tell us your verdict in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery we put to the test.
